.SH "DDC *.cfg FILE SYNTAX"
.IX Header "DDC *.cfg FILE SYNTAX"
This manpage describes the syntax of
the \fIddc_local_corpora.cfg\fR and \fIddc_server.cfg\fR
files (\*(L"cfg-files\*(R") used by the \s-1DDC\s0 corpus indexing system.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Local cfg-files (\fIddc_local_corpora.cfg\fR) defines the terminal (\*(L"leaf\*(R") nodes
of a \s-1DDC\s0 server dataflow tree which are to be handled by a single server process.
Server cfg-files (\fIddc_server.cfg\fR) associate each local leaf node
with at least one non-terminal (\*(L"branch\*(R") node, and may also incorporate
external leaf or branch nodes as \*(L"opaque\*(R" nodes, as well as define
\&\*(L"internal\*(R" branch nodes for the server dataflow tree.
Prior to \s-1DDC\s0 v2.1.0, at most one branch-node could be declared
in \fIddc_server.cfg\fR, and all leaf nodes had to be explicitly declared,
since branch nodes could not be queried as opaque leaf-like nodes.
.PP
All \s-1DDC\s0 cfg-files share a common basic format.
Files are line-based, containing one server-node record per line.
Blank lines (containing only whitespace) and comments
(lines beginning with a hash-mark (\f(CW\*(C`#\*(C'\fR) or double-slash (\f(CW\*(C`//\*(C'\fR)) are ignored.
Each content line should contain 3 or 4 fields separated by whitespace:
.PP
.Vb 1
\& LABEL  ADDR  PORT  PATH
.Ve
.SS "Label"
.IX Subsection "Label"
The first field specifies a symbolic \fI\s-1LABEL\s0\fR for the server node.
Node labels should be unique within the scope of a single cfg-file.
.PP
For server-config files \f(CW\*(C`ddc_server.cfg\*(C'\fR, if \fI\s-1LABEL\s0\fR is either
the string \f(CW\*(C`server\*(C'\fR or begins with the prefix \f(CW\*(C`server:\*(C'\fR,
the corresponding server-node will be created as a
branch-node (a \f(CW\*(C`CDDCBranchServer\*(C'\fR object representing a non-terminal node in the server dataflow tree).
Otherwise, the node is treated as an opaque (terminal) leaf-node.
.SS "Addr"
.IX Subsection "Addr"
The second field specifies the address \fI\s-1ADDR\s0\fR to be bound by a branch-node
and/or that to be queried for a leaf-node.  If \fI\s-1ADDR\s0\fR is the
special string \f(CW0.0.0.0\fR, all available interfaces will be bound for
a branch-node, while the loopback interface (\f(CW127.0.0.1\fR) will be queried.
.SS "Port"
.IX Subsection "Port"
The third field specifies the \s-1TCP\s0 port-number \fI\s-1PORT\s0\fR to be bound
by a branch-node and/or to be queried for a leaf-node.
.SS "Path"
.IX Subsection "Path"
The meaning fourth and final field \fI\s-1PATH\s0\fR differs between \fIddc_local_corpora.cfg\fR and \fIddc_server.cfg\fR.
.PP
For \fIddc_local_corpora.cfg\fR, \fI\s-1PATH\s0\fR is required, and specifies the local path to the associated
\&\s-1DDC\s0 project file (\f(CW\*(C`*.con\*(C'\fR), relative to the \s-1DDC\s0 runtime root directory as stored
in the environment variable \f(CW$RML\fR
.PP
For \fIddc_server.cfg\fR, \fI\s-1PATH\s0\fR is optional.  If non-empty, it specifies
the \fI\s-1LABEL\s0\fR of the node's parent in the dataflow tree,
which should be a branch node.  If empty, the most recently declared
branch-node is used as the parent.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
.SS "Example 1: Flat Dataflow"
.IX Subsection "Example 1: Flat Dataflow"
.IP "ddc_local_corpora.cfg" 4
.IX Item "ddc_local_corpora.cfg"
.Vb 4
\& sub1  0.0.0.0  50001  index/sub1/sub1.con
\& sub2  0.0.0.0  50002  index/sub1/sub2.con
\& sub3  0.0.0.0  50003  index/sub1/sub3.con
\& sub4  0.0.0.0  50004  index/sub1/sub4.con
.Ve
.IP "ddc_server.cfg" 4
.IX Item "ddc_server.cfg"
.Vb 5
\& server 0.0.0.0   50000
\& sub1   127.0.0.1 50001
\& sub2   127.0.0.1 50002
\& sub3   127.0.0.1 50003
\& sub4   127.0.0.1 50004
.Ve
.PP
This example defines a basic \*(L"flat\*(R" dataflow tree with exactly 1 branch node (\*(L"server\*(R"),
analagous to the dataflow trees supported by \s-1DDC\s0 < v2.1.0.
.PP
.Vb 4
\&         server
\&   _\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_
\&   |     |     |     |
\&  sub1  sub2  sub3  sub4
.Ve
.SS "Example 2: External Leaf Nodes / Meta-Server"
.IX Subsection "Example 2: External Leaf Nodes / Meta-Server"
.IP "ddc_local_corpora.cfg" 4
.IX Item "ddc_local_corpora.cfg"
(empty)
.IP "ddc_server.cfg" 4
.IX Item "ddc_server.cfg"
.Vb 5
\& server 0.0.0.0   60000
\& ext1   127.0.0.1 60001
\& ext2   127.0.0.1 60002
\& ext3   127.0.0.1 60003
\& ext4   127.0.0.1 60004
.Ve
.PP
This example defines a basic \*(L"flat\*(R" dataflow tree with exactly 1 branch node
as above, but without any local leaf nodes (sometimes called a \*(L"meta-server\*(R").
All leaf nodes are assumed to be handled by external processes.
.PP
.Vb 4
\&             server
\&   _\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_
\&   |       |       |       |
\& (ext1)  (ext2)  (ext3)  (ext4)
.Ve
.SS "Example 3: Internal Branch Nodes"
.IX Subsection "Example 3: Internal Branch Nodes"
.IP "ddc_local_corpora.cfg" 4
.IX Item "ddc_local_corpora.cfg"
.Vb 4
\& sub1  0.0.0.0  50001  index/sub1/sub1.con
\& sub2  0.0.0.0  50002  index/sub1/sub2.con
\& sub3  0.0.0.0  50003  index/sub1/sub3.con
\& sub4  0.0.0.0  50004  index/sub1/sub4.con
.Ve
.IP "ddc_server.cfg" 4
.IX Item "ddc_server.cfg"
.Vb 1
\& server:root 0.0.0.0   50000
\&
\& server:int1 0.0.0.0   50010 server:root
\& sub1        127.0.0.1 50001 server:int1
\& sub2        127.0.0.1 50002 server:int1
\&
\& server:int2 0.0.0.0   50020 server:root
\& sub3        127.0.0.1 50003 server:int2
\& sub4        127.0.0.1 50004 server:int2
.Ve
.IP "ddc_server.cfg (alternate)" 4
.IX Item "ddc_server.cfg (alternate)"
Server declarations for leaf-nodes can be omitted if they are
declared within the scope of the associated branch-nodes:
.Sp
.Vb 1
\& server:root 0.0.0.0   50000
\&
\& server:int1 0.0.0.0   50010 server:root
\& sub1        127.0.0.1 50001
\& sub2        127.0.0.1 50002
\&
\& server:int2 0.0.0.0   50020 server:root
\& sub3        127.0.0.1 50003
\& sub4        127.0.0.1 50004
.Ve
.PP
This example defines a binary-branching dataflow tree of depth 2,
containing 2 internal branch nodes (\*(L"server:int1\*(R" and \*(L"server:int2\*(R")
in addition to the root node (\*(L"server:root\*(R").  Requires ddc >= v2.1.0.
.PP
.Vb 7
\&         server:root
\&       _\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_\|_
\&       |             |
\&  server:int1    server:int2
\&   _\|_\|_|_\|_\|_         _\|_\|_|_\|_\|_
\&   |     |         |     |
\&  sub1  sub2      sub3  sub4
.Ve
